--- error -- the error-raising primitive contract (ADR-0092 gap (a)).
---
--- `error.raise(v)` fails the current evaluation loudly: it never
--- returns, and the host surfaces the payload as a normal eval error
--- (`EvalError::Other` -> `LangError::Engine`). This is the primitive the
--- pure-handl stdlib needs for contract violations -- `vec.pop`/`peek` on
--- an empty collection, `result` unwrap-style functions, and eventually
--- the pure-handl `assert.*`/`snapshot.match` implementations.
---
--- Payload: any value. A `String` payload becomes the error message
--- verbatim; any other value is carried as its JSON serialization in the
--- message. (Structured error *values* -- a `__tag__`ged `err` payload
--- that survives capture -- are a capture-side concern; there is still no
--- error-capture primitive, see ADR-0092 gap (b).)
---
--- `raise` is an irreducible atom: aborting evaluation cannot be
--- expressed over the eval vocabulary, so it stays a native `op`
--- (`plugin-lib-stdlib::ops::error`). Inside `.hnl` sources it is called
--- as `error.raise(msg)` -- the unbound `error` var falls back to the
--- `"error"` module path, exactly like `type.of`/`tag.tag`.
---
--- `error.try(f)` calls a thunk and captures raised errors as a `result`
--- value: `{"__tag__":"ok","value":v}` on success or
--- `{"__tag__":"err","value":msg}` on failure. This closes ADR-0092
--- gap (b) and makes `assert.throws`/`test.run` expressible in handl.

cap "error.raise"
cap "error.try"

--- error.raise -- fail the current evaluation with the given payload.
op "error.raise" : Value -> a

--- error.try -- call a thunk and return a `result` tag.
op "error.try" : Fn -> Value

handle "error.raise" with rust_error_raise
handle "error.try" with rust_error_try
